    "description": "What: CE-11072 (docs/designs/engineering/DESIGN_Breachable_Obstacle_Walls.md §6) — on the synthetic terrain te-osm-bridge (a two-way road along y 100 with a SUMO net), a 12 m SANDBAG feature wall, 1 m high, stands across the road on the west bank at x 50 (y 94..106). A scenario wall closes the lanes it crosses edge to edge (CE-11070), so 'Car' — a vehicle handed to SUMO (a road convoy of one, Mode Traffic) driving east to (180, 98.25) — cannot pass it. After 20 s 'Dozer' is ordered to clear the wall at (50, 98.25), the eastbound lane's centre: its blade cuts a hull-wide Passage (>= 4.2 m), the rest of the wall stands, the eastbound lane re-opens, and the car drives on. Judge: the car never passes the wall line before the dozer reaches it; the dozer cuts and drives through; the car reaches the east bank."
  },
